{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nconst int N = 505;\nint n, m, M;\nlong long dp[N], f[N], C[N][N];\nlong long d[N][N], fd[N][N];\n\n// Helper to access fd/d with fallback for negative index\ninline long long get_fd(int i, int j, int k) {\n    return (i-k-1 >= 0) ? fd[i-k-1][j-k] : 1;\n}\ninline long long get_d(int i, int j, int k) {\n    return (i-k-1 >= 0) ? d[i-k-1][j-k] : 0;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    scanf(\"%d %d %d\", &n, &m, &M);\n    f[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i <= n; ++i) {\n        C[i][0] = C[i][i] = 1;\n        for (int j = 1; j < i; ++j)\n            C[i][j] = (C[i-1][j] + C[i-1][j-1]) % M;\n    }\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 1; j <= i; ++j) {\n            f[i] = (f[i] + f[j-1] * f[i-j] % M * C[i-1][j-1] % M * (i+1)) % M;\n        }\n    }\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 1; j <= i; ++j) {\n            int s = 0;\n            for (int k = 1; k <= i; ++k) s += abs(k-j);\n            dp[i] = (dp[i] + dp[j-1] * f[i-j] % M * C[i-1][j-1] % M * (i+1) \n                     + f[j-1] * dp[i-j] % M * C[i-1][j-1] % M * (i+1) \n                     + s * f[j-1] % M * f[i-j] % M * C[i-1][j-1]) % M;\n        }\n    }\n    fd[0][0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j <= min(m, i); ++j) {\n            fd[i][j] = fd[i-1][j];\n            d[i][j] = d[i-1][j];\n            for (int k = 1; k <= j; ++k) {\n                long long fdPrev = get_fd(i, j, k);\n                long long dPrev = get_d(i, j, k);\n                fd[i][j] = (fd[i][j] + fdPrev * f[k] % M * C[j][k]) % M;\n                d[i][j] = (d[i][j] + (fdPrev * dp[k] + dPrev * f[k]) % M * C[j][k]) % M;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    cout << (d[n][m] % M + M) % M;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\ndef solve():\n    import sys\n    input_data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not input_data:\n        return\n    n, m, M = map(int, input_data[:3])\n    # f and dp arrays\n    f = [0] * (n + 1)\n    f[0] = 1\n    # C[n][k] combinations modulo M\n    C = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        C[i][0] = C[i][i] = 1\n        for j in range(1, i):\n            C[i][j] = (C[i-1][j] + C[i-1][j-1]) % M\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    # compute f and dp\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # f[i]\n            f[i] = (f[i] + f[j-1] * f[i-j] % M * C[i-1][j-1] % M * (i+1)) % M\n            # dp[i]\n            s = 0\n            for k in range(1, i + 1):\n                s += abs(k - j)\n            dp[i] = (dp[i] + dp[j-1] * f[i-j] % M * C[i-1][j-1] % M * (i+1)\n                     + f[j-1] * dp[i-j] % M * C[i-1][j-1] % M * (i+1)\n                     + s * f[j-1] % M * f[i-j] % M * C[i-1][j-1]) % M\n    # fd and d arrays\n    fd = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    d = [[0] * (m + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    fd[0][0] = 1\n    # helper functions for safe access\n    def get_fd(i, j, k):\n        # returns fd[i-k-1][j-k] if index >= 0 else 1\n        if i - k - 1 >= 0:\n            return fd[i - k - 1][j - k]\n        else:\n            return 1\n    def get_d(i, j, k):\n        if i - k - 1 >= 0:\n            return d[i - k - 1][j - k]\n        else:\n            return 0\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        max_j = min(m, i)\n        for j in range(max_j + 1):\n            fd[i][j] = fd[i-1][j]\n            d[i][j] = d[i-1][j]\n            for k in range(1, j + 1):\n                fd_prev = get_fd(i, j, k)\n                d_prev = get_d(i, j, k)\n                fd[i][j] = (fd[i][j] + fd_prev * f[k] % M * C[j][k]) % M\n                d[i][j] = (d[i][j] + (fd_prev * dp[k] + d_prev * f[k]) % M * C[j][k]) % M\n    ans = d[n][m] % M\n    print(ans)\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0055151209235191345, -8.821448318485636e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -8.511180931236595e-05, -0.5932409763336182, -0.2024574875831604, -0.006723874714225531, -3.981510963058099e-05, -0.10036412626504898, -5.9126061387360096e-05, -0.001086479052901268, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.1369909793138504, -0.20142795145511627, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.397406908334233e-05, 0.0, -0.038042102009058, -3.099436753473128e-06, -0.07889062911272049, -1.0132738680113107e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.264974000354414e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.660974445869215e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00015841660206206143, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.029788371175527573, -0.25193867087364197, -3.8742269680369645e-05, -2.47952248173533e-05, -0.00017510310863144696, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.6954811548639555e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, -0.19319504499435425, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.16025488078594208, -0.25200530886650085, -0.6826353669166565, -